<?php
/**
 * Spartrak_Catalog — shared Product Card.
 *
 * ONE template for every product-card use on the site: the PLP/category
 * grid and search-results grid (each Spartrak theme's own
 * Magento_Catalog/templates/product/list.phtml, which passes the page's
 * real Magento\Catalog\Block\Product\ListProduct instance as `list_block`
 * so this template can use its native getAddToCartUrl()) and every
 * dashboard-driven homepage product section (Spartrak_Homepage's
 * Block\Section\ProductCarousel::renderCard — the CMS-block homepage that
 * used to call this template was removed in the 2026-08-27 homepage pass).
 * Never build a page-specific card template — extend this file instead, per
 * 04-COMPONENT-INVENTORY.md's "Card - Product" single-component rule.
 *
 * --- FIGMA PASS 2026-08-26 -------------------------------------------
 * Rebuilt against the real Figma nodes, read live via the Figma MCP
 * server (file 6FRlQfPIncVUvNiJLn2kbT):
 *
 *   Card - Product            569:13667 (plain) / 569:13704 (discounted)
 *   Image Container           569:13705      1:1, bg/field, overflow clip
 *   Buttons overlay           569:13707      absolute, p-12, space-between
 *   Promo Label               569:13708      feedback/danger pill, h28
 *   Like Button               718:25231      40px white circle + heart 20
 *   Content Container         569:13714      gap 12, px 4, pb 12
 *   Name                      569:13719      Heading/H4 18/1.3, 2-line clamp
 *   Rating Container          569:13720      5x20 stars + value + count
 *   Price and Button          569:13742      space-between
 *   Primary Buttons           718:25242      36px action/primary circle
 *   Price                     569:13744      old (price-sale, struck) + final
 *
 * --- CSS LIVES IN _product-card.less (moved 2026-08-27) --------------
 * This template previously carried the card's entire stylesheet in an
 * inline <style> block, plus three icons built as data: URIs. Both are
 * gone: the rules are in the theme's
 * web/css/source/components/_product-card.less, where they are compiled,
 * minified, comment-stripped and cached once instead of being re-sent
 * inside every HTML response. See that file's header for the move's
 * rationale and for the specificity note that came with it.
 *
 * The three icons it referenced are the EXACT assets Figma exports for
 * these nodes and are now linked from the LESS as ordinary cacheable
 * files; each was byte-compared against the previously inlined path data,
 * so nothing about the rendering changed:
 *   heart.svg  == Figma 718:25608 (821 B, stroke #1A144F = icon/default)
 *   plus.svg   == Figma 718:25614 (472 B, 12.9167 box incl. stroke bleed)
 *   star.svg   == Figma 569:13722 path, flat fill so it can be masked and
 *                 tinted with the two real rating tokens
 *
 * THREE DELIBERATE, DOCUMENTED DEVIATIONS FROM THE FIGMA RENDER — see
 * CLAUDE.md section 3 "PERFORMANCE + PIXEL ACCURACY" and section 4:
 *
 *  1. RATING STARS. In Figma every card's star row sits in the component's
 *     empty state: all five stars sample to exactly #f8e5a5
 *     (= --color-rating-empty) on the 1:1 PNG export, even on a 4.8-rated
 *     card, and the 5th star's own mask asset carries #EEBD1D at 40% alpha
 *     (which resolves to that same #f8e5a5 over white). The component is
 *     clearly BUILT for fractional fill — its 5th star is a masked partial
 *     — the instances just were not set. Shipping the literal render would
 *     be a rating widget that never indicates the rating. So the stars fill
 *     proportionally, using only the two colours that already exist in that
 *     same component's own assets: --color-action-accent (#eebd1d, the
 *     filled half of the partial-star export) and --color-rating-empty
 *     (#f8e5a5). Deleting the background-image declaration on
 *     .spartrak-card__stars in _product-card.less reverts to the literal
 *     render.
 *
 *  2. PROMO BADGE "GLOW". Figma node 569:13709 puts a 30deg-rotated,
 *     2px-blurred, soft-light, 18%-opacity white shine inside the badge.
 *     Measured on the 1:1 PNG export of node 569:13708 it moves the badge
 *     from #d54033 to #d64134 — a 1/255 delta, below perceptual threshold —
 *     while costing a blur + mix-blend-mode compositing layer on every
 *     discounted card in the grid. Omitted on the section-13 rule that less
 *     paint wins when the pixels are indistinguishable. Re-add if a design
 *     review disagrees.
 *
 *  3. BRAND LINE. The previous pass rendered the `brand` attribute here.
 *     The Figma card has no brand line — the component's `Label` slot
 *     (718:25220) is hidden="true" on all twelve instances — so it is gone,
 *     along with its per-card getAttributeText() call.
 *
 * ONE GENUINE DATA GAP, NOT FAKED: Figma's rating line reads "(54 مبيع)" —
 * "(54 SOLD)", not "(54 reviews)". Magento has no sold-quantity figure on a
 * product; it lives in the Reports aggregates. Rather than print a review
 * count under a "sold" label, this renders the real review count with the
 * real "(%1 reviews)" string (already translated in the theme's ar_EG.csv).
 * A sold-qty attribute + cron aggregate is backend work — see list.phtml.
 *
 * Price still renders through Magento's standard price-render pipeline
 * (Magento\Framework\Pricing\Render), which resolves to each theme's own
 * product/price/final_price.phtml override — that is where the zero-price
 * "Price on request" fallback lives, so every caller of this card gets it.
 *
 * @var \Magento\Framework\View\Element\Template $block
 */

/** @var \Magento\Catalog\Block\Product\ListProduct|null $listBlock */
$listBlock = $block->getData('list_block');
/** @var \Magento\Catalog\Model\Product $product */
$product = $block->getData('product');

if (!$product) {
    return;
}

// Position in the grid, passed by list.phtml. Drives the LCP treatment
// below — CLAUDE.md sections 11/12: the first row of a PLP is above the
// fold, so those images must NOT be lazy-loaded, and exactly one of them
// (the first) gets fetchpriority="high". Everything below stays lazy.
// Defaults to a below-fold value so any caller that does not pass an index
// (e.g. the homepage rail) keeps the safe, lazy behaviour.
$index = $block->hasData('index') ? (int) $block->getData('index') : 99;
$aboveFold = $index < 4;

/**
 * VARIANT — one component, two layouts (added by the HOMEPAGE PASS 2026-08-27).
 *
 * Figma's `Card - Product` is a single component with a horizontal instance:
 * node 746:37718, used inside the homepage showcase item (595:14852) at
 * 532x140 — image on the inline-start side, name on one line, no add-to-cart
 * button, and the wishlist heart moved out of the image overlay and into the
 * content row.
 *
 * That is a VARIANT of this component in the design file, so it is a variant
 * here too, not a second template. 04-COMPONENT-INVENTORY.md's single
 * "Card - Product" rule is about not forking the card per page — a variant the
 * design itself defines is the opposite of a fork.
 *
 *   'grid'       (default) — the PLP / search / homepage-rail card
 *   'horizontal'           — the showcase card
 *
 * Everything upstream of this line (price, rating, discount, wishlist) is
 * computed identically for both; only the markup below branches.
 */
$variant = (string) ($block->getData('variant') ?: 'grid');
$isHorizontal = $variant === 'horizontal';

$imageHelper = $this->helper(\Magento\Catalog\Helper\Image::class);
$image = $imageHelper->init($product, 'category_page_grid');

// --- Discount badge (real Magento pricing data, never fabricated) -------
// Figma 569:13708 "خصم 15%". Percentage off = regular vs final price, i.e.
// a real special_price / catalog price rule. No special price, no badge.
$discountPercent = 0;
try {
    $priceInfo = $product->getPriceInfo();
    $regularAmount = (float) $priceInfo->getPrice('regular_price')->getAmount()->getValue();
    $finalAmount = (float) $priceInfo->getPrice('final_price')->getAmount()->getValue();
    if ($regularAmount > 0 && $finalAmount > 0 && $finalAmount < $regularAmount) {
        $discountPercent = (int) round((1 - ($finalAmount / $regularAmount)) * 100);
    }
} catch (\Exception $e) {
    $discountPercent = 0;
}

// --- Rating (real review data) ------------------------------------------
// Magento_Review appends rating_summary/reviews_count to every product in a
// listing collection via CatalogBlockProductCollectionBeforeToHtmlObserver,
// so this needs no extra query. rating_summary is already a 0-100 percent,
// which is exactly what the star mask below wants.
$ratingPercent = (int) $product->getRatingSummary();
$reviewsCount = (int) $product->getReviewsCount();
$ratingValue = $ratingPercent > 0 ? number_format($ratingPercent / 20, 1) : '';

$priceHtml = '';
try {
    $priceRender = $block->getLayout()->getBlock('product.price.render.default');
    if (!$priceRender) {
        $priceRender = $block->getLayout()->createBlock(
            \Magento\Framework\Pricing\Render::class,
            'product.price.render.default',
            ['data' => ['price_render_handle' => 'catalog_product_prices']]
        );
    }
    $priceHtml = $priceRender->render(
        \Magento\Catalog\Pricing\Price\FinalPrice::PRICE_CODE,
        $product,
        ['zone' => \Magento\Framework\Pricing\Render::ZONE_ITEM_LIST]
    );
} catch (\Exception $e) {
    $priceHtml = '';
}

// Wishlist heart (Figma 718:25231). Reuses Magento's own native ajax
// add-to-wishlist block/template — the exact one every Luma listing card
// uses — so the [data-action="add-to-wishlist"] behaviour comes free from
// Magento_Wishlist's own JS and this template adds none.
$wishlistHtml = '';
try {
    $wishlistHtml = $block->getLayout()
        ->createBlock(\Magento\Wishlist\Block\Catalog\Product\ProductList\Item\AddTo\Wishlist::class)
        ->setProduct($product)
        ->toHtml();
} catch (\Exception $e) {
    $wishlistHtml = '';
}


?>
<?php if ($isHorizontal) : ?>
    <?php /*
      HORIZONTAL VARIANT — Figma 746:37718.
      DOM order is [content, media] so that under dir="rtl" the 140px image
      lands on the inline-start (right) edge exactly as the design composes
      it, and mirrors correctly on an English store view — same technique as
      the grid variant's overlay row, no RTL stylesheet involved.
      No add-to-cart form and no promo badge: neither exists on this variant
      in Figma, and the whole card is a link to the product.
    */ ?>
    <div class="spartrak-card spartrak-card--horizontal">
        <div class="spartrak-card__content">
            <?php if (trim($wishlistHtml)) : ?>
                <div class="spartrak-card__wishlist"><?= /* @noEscape */ $wishlistHtml ?></div>
            <?php endif; ?>
            <div class="spartrak-card__heading">
                <div class="spartrak-card__name-wrap">
                    <a class="spartrak-card__name" href="<?= $block->escapeUrl($product->getProductUrl()) ?>">
                        <?= $block->escapeHtml($product->getName()) ?>
                    </a>
                </div>
                <?php if ($ratingPercent > 0) : ?>
                    <div class="spartrak-card__rating">
                        <span class="spartrak-card__stars"
                              style="--spartrak-rating-fill: <?= (int) $ratingPercent ?>%"
                              role="img"
                              aria-label="<?= $block->escapeHtmlAttr(__('Rated %1 out of 5', $ratingValue)) ?>"></span>
                        <span class="spartrak-card__rating-value"><?= $block->escapeHtml($ratingValue) ?></span>
                        <?php if ($reviewsCount > 0) : ?>
                            <span class="spartrak-card__rating-count" dir="auto"><?= $block->escapeHtml(__('(%1 reviews)', $reviewsCount)) ?></span>
                        <?php endif; ?>
                    </div>
                <?php endif; ?>
                <div class="spartrak-card__price"><?= /* @noEscape */ $priceHtml ?></div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="spartrak-card__media">
            <a class="spartrak-card__image-link"
               href="<?= $block->escapeUrl($product->getProductUrl()) ?>"
               tabindex="-1"
               aria-hidden="true">
                <img
                    class="spartrak-card__image"
                    src="<?= $block->escapeUrl($image->getUrl()) ?>"
                    alt=""
                    width="<?= $block->escapeHtmlAttr($image->getWidth()) ?>"
                    height="<?= $block->escapeHtmlAttr($image->getHeight()) ?>"
                    loading="<?= $aboveFold ? 'eager' : 'lazy' ?>"
                    decoding="async"
                />
            </a>
        </div>
    </div>
<?php else : ?>
<div class="spartrak-card">
    <div class="spartrak-card__media">
        <!--
          The wishlist button is a real <a> — it CANNOT nest inside the
          image's own <a>. Media is a plain <div>; the image link and the
          overlay row are siblings stacked by CSS. The image link is
          aria-hidden/untabbable because the product name below is the
          accessible link to the same URL — one target, not two.
        -->
        <a class="spartrak-card__image-link"
           href="<?= $block->escapeUrl($product->getProductUrl()) ?>"
           tabindex="-1"
           aria-hidden="true">
            <img
                class="spartrak-card__image"
                src="<?= $block->escapeUrl($image->getUrl()) ?>"
                alt=""
                width="<?= $block->escapeHtmlAttr($image->getWidth()) ?>"
                height="<?= $block->escapeHtmlAttr($image->getHeight()) ?>"
                loading="<?= $aboveFold ? 'eager' : 'lazy' ?>"
                decoding="async"
                <?php if ($index === 0) : ?>fetchpriority="high"<?php endif; ?>
            />
        </a>
        <?php if (trim($wishlistHtml) || $discountPercent > 0) : ?>
            <div class="spartrak-card__actions">
                <?php if (trim($wishlistHtml)) : ?>
                    <div class="spartrak-card__wishlist"><?= /* @noEscape */ $wishlistHtml ?></div>
                <?php endif; ?>
                <?php if ($discountPercent > 0) : ?>
                    <span class="spartrak-card__promo"><?= $block->escapeHtml(__('Discount %1', $discountPercent . '%')) ?></span>
                <?php endif; ?>
            </div>
        <?php endif; ?>
    </div>
    <div class="spartrak-card__body">
        <div class="spartrak-card__content">
            <div class="spartrak-card__heading">
                <div class="spartrak-card__name-wrap">
                    <a class="spartrak-card__name" href="<?= $block->escapeUrl($product->getProductUrl()) ?>">
                        <?= $block->escapeHtml($product->getName()) ?>
                    </a>
                </div>
                <?php if ($ratingPercent > 0) : ?>
                    <div class="spartrak-card__rating">
                        <span class="spartrak-card__stars"
                              style="--spartrak-rating-fill: <?= (int) $ratingPercent ?>%"
                              role="img"
                              aria-label="<?= $block->escapeHtmlAttr(__('Rated %1 out of 5', $ratingValue)) ?>"></span>
                        <span class="spartrak-card__rating-value"><?= $block->escapeHtml($ratingValue) ?></span>
                        <?php if ($reviewsCount > 0) : ?>
                            <span class="spartrak-card__rating-count" dir="auto"><?= $block->escapeHtml(__('(%1 reviews)', $reviewsCount)) ?></span>
                        <?php endif; ?>
                    </div>
                <?php endif; ?>
            </div>
            <div class="spartrak-card__price-row">
                <div class="spartrak-card__price"><?= /* @noEscape */ $priceHtml ?></div>
                <?php if ($listBlock) : ?>
                    <?php /*
                      data-mage-init is what makes this an AJAX add-to-cart.
                      Without it the form does a plain POST and the whole page
                      reloads — which is exactly what happened on the homepage,
                      where (unlike the PLP) nothing else was initialising the
                      widget. Core puts the same attribute on the same form in
                      Magento_Catalog::product/list.phtml, so this is its own
                      mechanism, not a workaround.
                    */ ?>
                    <form class="spartrak-card__form"
                          data-role="tocart-form"
                          data-mage-init='{"catalogAddToCart": {}}'
                          action="<?= $block->escapeUrl($listBlock->getAddToCartUrl($product)) ?>"
                          method="post">
                        <?= /* @noEscape */ $block->getBlockHtml('formkey') ?>
                        <input type="hidden" name="product" value="<?= (int) $product->getId() ?>" />
                        <input type="hidden" name="qty" value="1" />
                        <button type="submit"
                                class="spartrak-card__add-to-cart"
                                title="<?= $block->escapeHtmlAttr(__('Add to Cart')) ?>">
                            <span><?= $block->escapeHtml(__('Add to Cart')) ?></span>
                        </button>
                    </form>
                <?php endif; ?>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<?php endif; ?>
